on topic branch ralph/codex-slash-commands. Test command: pnpm --filter '{packages/happy-cli}' exec vitest run 2>&1 | tee /tmp/codexu-slash.log. Single commit; update plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md Gap 5 section to mark shipped.\""
plans/overview.html:1050:                    "planPrompt": "/plan-with-ralph \"Gap 6 from plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md — defensive plan-mode mapping on codex path. Today packages/happy-cli/src/codex/cliArgs.ts VALID_CODEX_REMOTE_PERMISSION_MODES (re-exported as VALID_REMOTE_PERMISSION_MODES in runCodex.ts:251) is restricted to default, read-only, safe-yolo, yolo — `plan` arriving from the mobile UI is silently ignored (runCodex.ts:287-294); the local CLI flag path falls into the defensive branch in executionPolicy.ts:24,39 returning untrusted+workspace-write. There is no ExitPlanMode codex tool. PREREQUISITE (operator-gated): confirm v1 scope is option (a) DEFENSIVE — map `plan` → codex `read-only` sandbox in executionPolicy.ts, AND emit a UI hint (session-event 'message') on first plan-mode entry: 'Plan mode on codex is approximated as read-only; ExitPlanMode tool is not available.' If operator wants option (b) overlay-crate full parity instead, defer this task and open a separate `codex-plan-mode-overlay` ralph command that lands an overlay crate codex/codex-rs-overlay/codex-plan-mode/ providing real plan-mode parity (model gets an exit_plan_mode tool, mode transitions on tool call) — spike upstream codex's tool-registration seam first. Acceptance for v1 (a): switching a codex session to plan mode results in sandbox: read-only, approvalPolicy: never, and the user sees the explanatory message; the existing mobile-UI plan-mode badge still renders correctly. Cross-package typecheck green. Test command: pnpm --filter '{packages/happy-cli}' exec vitest run 2>&1 | tee /tmp/codexu-plan-mode.log. Single commit referencing audit Gap 6. Update plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md Gap 6 section to mark v1-defensive shipped; flag v2-overlay as still deferred. Workflow: codexu worktree at .worktrees/codex-plan-mode-defensive/ on topic branch ralph/codex-plan-mode-defensive off origin/main.\""
plans/overview.html:1069:                    "planPrompt": "/plan-with-ralph \"Bundle the 4 Low-severity codex-parity gaps from plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md into a single polish PR. The audit recommended this packaging explicitly: '8. Gaps 8, 9, 11, 12 are all small and can land in a single polish PR if desired.' One commit per gap so each can be reverted independently.\n\nGAP 8 — codex-tool-gating-partial. Track allowedTools/disallowedTools in codex EnhancedMode (runCodex.ts:96-100, currently restricted to { permissionMode, model, thinkingLevel }); at startThread, filter the mcpServers entries (whole-server granularity — drop entries whose tools are entirely disallowed). True per-tool-within-server filtering deferred to a follow-up overlay crate.\n\nGAP 9 — codex-args-passthrough. Add repeatable --codex-arg <flag> to packages/happy-cli/src/codex/cliArgs.ts (alongside existing --effort, --model, --permission-mode, --codex-transport, --resume). Forward to the `codex app-server` spawn argv. Power-user escape hatch — document in packages/happy-cli/CLAUDE.md that structured flags are preferred.\n\nGAP 11 — codex-statusline-metadata-mirror. Extend the metadata-merge in both runCodex.ts:796-800 AND resumeExistingThread.ts to include model, modelProvider, approvalPolicy, sandbox, reasoningEffort from NewConversationResponse / ResumeConversationResponse (codexAppServerTypes.ts:35-47) — currently only codexThreadId is written. Match the Claude side's mergeSDKInitMetadata semantics.\n\nGAP 12 — codex-sdk-init-metadata-mirror. Investigate the codex initialize RPC's full response shape (server capabilities, available tools, slash commands) and propagate those into Session.metadata so the mobile app can render them. Likely a small extension of the metadata-merge from Gap 11.\n\nCONFLICT WARNING: all 4 gaps touch runCodex.ts and/or resumeExistingThread.ts — sequence after mcp-discovery / codex-claude-md-autoload / codex-system-prompts / codex-hooks-parity have landed to avoid rebase churn. Workflow: codexu worktree at .worktrees/codex-polish-lows/ on topic branch ralph/codex-polish-lows off origin/main. 4 commits (one per gap), all referencing the corresponding audit-doc section. Cross-package typecheck green. Each gap has its own acceptance test. Update plans/codex-agent-parity-audit.md Gap 8/9/11/12 sections to mark shipped.\""
plans/overview.html:1275:      "summary": "Filled the previously empty explorer.toml stub at codex/external/repos/codex-patched/codex-rs/core/src/agent/builtins/explorer.toml with a paraphrased Explore prompt (1538 chars, no brand strings, no 6-word verbatim spans from Claude's source — license review approved per plans/native-agent-parity.md §4 posture). Codex-side commit e9fa64a0 on feat/explorer-role-prompt: 3 files +108/-7 — explorer.toml content, role_tests.rs updated (renamed test + new invariant test + session-flags assert + SANDBOX PATCH markers), codex/docs/implementation/patch-surface.md §17 new + §14 row 21. codexu pointer-bump d279d49d (1 file, +1/-1) bumping codex submodule from 17999363 → e9fa64a0. 9 of 10 stories closed (US-006 smoke deferred to post-publish workflow — local rebuild needs LLVM/xwin/V8 env; will be covered by /publish-sandbox-patch + /verify when run). License posture verified at <job_dir>/license-review-approval.md. First piece of the native-agent-parity follow-up wave to ship — no role.rs match-arm change needed (file already wired)."
plans/overview.html:1315:      "summary": "No-op merge finding (acceptance path b). Codex's worker role is description-only (role.rs:382-394, config_file: None) — there's no developer_instructions layer to merge Claude's safety rails into. The two real gaps (Claude's 'NEVER create files unless absolutely necessary' + 'NEVER proactively create *.md / README files') ARE missing from codex's base prompt at gpt_5_2_prompt.md:156,158 (only weak abstract analogues), but the correct fix-site is launcher-injected additional_instructions (overlay path per AGENTS.override.md tenet 1), not worker-only enforcement which would skip the main-agent flow. Recommend: land port-explorer-prompt + port-plan-and-verification-roles first; revisit base-prompt overlay separately. plans/native-agent-parity.md §2.4 updated with the finding; §6 Q6 marked resolved."
